## Rules

- {{Where content is produced, and where it is published.}}
- {{Publication needs an explicit yes; never copy a file in place of writing a note.}}
- {{Never mirror: one artefact, one home.}}
- {{No vault guarantees in a work tree: no hash guard, no audit, no rollback, no drift check.}}
- {{Commit after project work — or state plainly that nothing is versioned.}}

## Extending the rules

Read and extend [conventions.md](conventions.md) — never grow this file. It holds the workflow,
the verification standard and the quirks that are too detailed for a page. Create it with the
first rule that does not fit here, and link it from this section in the same change: a dangling
link is worse than a short manual. In a vault it is a note (frontmatter, `topics`, body `Topics:`
footer, MoC entry); in a work tree it is a plain markdown file.

Keep this file to about a page: it is read on every entry, the rest only on demand. Where a
project skill holds the method instead, name it here and keep the facts in this file.

Write this file in the project's note language, not the language of the conversation that
created it.
